  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an integer array `nums`, output *the **largest possible sum** of elements of the array such that it is divisible by three*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [3,6,5,1,8]\nOutput: 18\nExplanation: Pick numbers 3, 6, 1 and 8 their sum is 18 (maximum sum divisible by 3).\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [4]\nOutput: 0\nExplanation: Since 4 is not divisible by 3, do not pick any number.\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,4,4]\nOutput: 12\nExplanation: Pick numbers 1, 3, 4 and 4 their sum is 12 (maximum sum divisible by 3).\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 4 * 104`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 104`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
